# Jira SCRUM Board Usage

Use the SCRUM Jira board at `https://ivancordonesnunez.atlassian.net/jira/software/projects/SCRUM/boards/1` as the **primary source of truth** for work items, tickets, and project status.

## Ticket Interpretation

- When a ticket key like `SCRUM-123` is mentioned, assume it refers to an issue on this Jira board.
- When implementing a ticket:
  - Align behavior, acceptance criteria, and edge cases with the Jira ticket description, comments, and attachments.
  - If requirements are ambiguous, make reasonable assumptions and clearly document them in code comments or commit messages.

## Communication & References

- When summarizing work related to a ticket, explicitly reference the ticket key (e.g., `SCRUM-123`) and this Jira board.
- Prefer phrasing like: “Implementation for `SCRUM-123` (see Jira SCRUM board)” when describing changes or plans.

## Scope

- Apply this guidance to **all conversations** in this project where Jira tickets, SCRUM items, or task IDs are referenced.

